### 9.3 Fault attribution

**Semantics**

1. A `fold_checked` overflow that occurs when contribution `k` is added is a fault of work-item `k`, at the step ordinal of its `reduce` statement, with the record that SPEC-04P.2 6.13.5 gives [SPEC-04P.2 R-6, IM-83].
2. A fault of the epilogue, the final check of a `sum` or a `min` or `max` with no contributions, occurs only when no work-item faulted, and epilogue faults are ordered after every work-item and among themselves by the declaration order of their targets, as SPEC-04P.2 6.13.5 states [SPEC-04P.2 R-7].
3. If the canonical fault is at work-item `k`, every work-item below `k` completed without a fault (SPEC-04P.2 6.13.6), so the partial result of a fold before `k`, which paragraph 1 uses, is fully defined [SPEC-04P.2 R-8].

**Examples**

4. The reduction comes before the division. At work-item 1 the fold overflows at step 1, before the division by `x[1] - 10 = 0` at step 4:

```cint tie_a.ci
kernel check[n](in I64[n] x, out I64[n] y, out I64 s) over [i: n] {
    reduce s = fold_checked(add, 0, x[i]);
    y[i] = div_round(100, x[i] - 10, floor);
}

void run() {
    I64[3] x = [9223372036854775807, 10, 0];
    I64[3] y;
    I64 s = 0;
    check(x, y, s);
}

run();
```

```text
fault[E_OVERFLOW]: the exact result is outside the type's range
  --> tie_a.ci:2:16
   |
 2 |     reduce s = fold_checked(add, 0, x[i]);
   |                ^ fold_checked.add.i64
   |
   = operation: fold_checked.add.i64
   = operand-count: 3
   = operand: I64 1
   = operand: I64 9223372036854775807
   = operand: I64 10
   = exact:   9223372036854775817
   = limit:   I64 9223372036854775807
   ...
   = address: tie_a.check, dispatch 0, phase 1, work-item 1, step 1
   ...
```

5. This example puts the same statements in the other order. The division at step 3 now comes before the reduction at step 5:

```cint tie_b.ci
kernel check[n](in I64[n] x, out I64[n] y, out I64 s) over [i: n] {
    y[i] = div_round(100, x[i] - 10, floor);
    reduce s = fold_checked(add, 0, x[i]);
}

void run() {
    I64[3] x = [9223372036854775807, 10, 0];
    I64[3] y;
    I64 s = 0;
    check(x, y, s);
}

run();
```

```text
fault[E_DIV_ZERO]: division by zero
  --> tie_b.ci:2:12
   |
 2 |     y[i] = div_round(100, x[i] - 10, floor);
