16. <a id="IM-132"></a><a id="IM-133"></a>The fault `E_NARROW` is raised by `x as T` when `v` is outside the range of `T`. The fault record holds the operation identifier `as.checked.s.t`, where `s` and `t` are the source and target types in lower case. A fixed-point type is written with `_` for its point (`q16_16`), and the identifier ends with `.mode` when the conversion rounds, whether its mode was written or not. The record holds one operand, the source value. Its exact result is `v`, which is a raw value when the target is a fixed-point type, and its limit is the bound of `T` that `v` crossed, a value of type `T`. Its position is the `as` token [IM-50, IM-68, IM-132, IM-133]. `as%` and `as?` raise no fault.

