> day 10: low 8.77, high 16.30, mean 12.92, spread 1.87
> day 11: low 9.37, high 16.88, mean 13.51, spread 1.94
...
> day 29: low 20.21, high 27.63, mean 24.31, spread 2.00
> day 30: low 20.81, high 28.23, mean 24.92, spread 1.88
```

The first eight days are unchanged and the month is complete. The fault is gone.

### fix 2: subtract the mean first

Put the `I32` version back. This time, square each reading's distance from the mean instead of the reading itself. The distances are a few hundred at most, so their squares are small:

```ci
I32 sum_of_squared_deviations[n](in I32[n] xs, I32 mean) {
    I32 total = 0;
    for i in 0..n {
        I32 dev = xs[i] - mean;
        total += dev * dev;
    }
    return total;
}
```

```ci
    I32 variance = sum_of_squared_deviations(day, mean) / 1_440;
    I32 spread = isqrt(variance);
```

